Elentrik Source License, version 1.0
Copyright (c) 2026 Steff Beckers. All rights reserved, except as expressly permitted by this license.

1. Definitions

   "The Software": the source code, documentation, designs, symbols, translations and all other files in
   this repository, and any modified version or derivative work of them, excluding the third-party
   software referred to in section 8.

   "The Licensor": Steff Beckers, the holder of the copyright in the Software.

   "You": the natural or legal person using the Software. If you act on behalf of a company or
   organisation, this license also applies to that company or organisation.

   "Production use": any use of the Software other than developing and testing the Software itself,
   whether for profit or not. This includes in any case: documenting real electrical installations,
   producing dossiers, diagrams or lists that are used outside development and testing, processing data
   of real customers or projects, and making the Software available over a network to anyone other than
   yourself.

   "Contribution": any modification, addition or other work that you submit to the Licensor for inclusion
   in the Software, including through a pull request in the official repository.

2. What you may do

   The Licensor grants you a non-exclusive, royalty-free, worldwide and non-transferable license, solely
   to contribute to the Software or to get to know it, to:

   a) view, read and study the Software;
   b) copy the Software, including by cloning or forking the repository;
   c) install and run the Software locally, on your own devices or in your own development and test
      environments, with test data;
   d) modify the Software and create derivative works of it;
   e) submit your modifications as a Contribution to the official repository;
   f) share your modifications publicly in a fork on GitHub, to prepare or discuss a Contribution, under
      this license.

3. What is prohibited without prior written permission

   Without the prior written permission of the Licensor, you may not, for the Software or any part of it:

   a) use it in production, for your own or for commercial purposes;
   b) offer or host it as a service, for customers, for third parties or for your own company or
      organisation;
   c) sell, resell, rent, lend, sublicense or otherwise make it available, whether for a fee or free of
      charge, except as permitted by section 2 f);
   d) use it to develop, improve or offer a competing product or service, or include parts of it in
      another product;
   e) use it without the copyright and license notices, or remove or alter those notices.

   A fork within GitHub arises from that platform's features and grants no rights beyond section 2. The
   official service at https://elentrik.app is the way to use Elentrik in production. For any other
   permission or a license: see section 13.

4. Conditions

   Every copy of the Software, modified or not, includes this license and the copyright notice. Modified
   versions are subject to this license; you may not apply any other license to them.

5. Contributions

   Before making a Contribution, you first accept the Contributor License Agreement in the file CLA.md. It
   sets out which rights in your Contributions you grant to the Licensor. The Licensor decides freely
   whether to include a Contribution.

6. Instance ping

   A deployed production build of the Software, outside the Licensor's official environments,
   automatically reports to https://elentrik.app: shortly after start-up and then once a day. The report
   contains a random identifier of the installation, the host name, the version, whether subscriptions
   are enabled and the number of organisations and users, but no names, email addresses or project
   content. The receiving server also stores the IP address of the report. Its purpose is visibility of
   installations running without a license. The file docs/instance-ping.md describes the ping in full,
   including how to disable it. Disabling the ping does not grant you any right beyond this license.

7. Trademarks

   This license grants no right to use the name "Elentrik", the logo or other marks of the Licensor,
   except to truthfully state the origin of the Software.

8. Third-party software

   Third-party software used or included by the Software is subject to the licenses of those third
   parties. This license does not apply to it. This includes:

   a) the dependencies listed in the package.json files;
   b) the code in apps/plan-editor/vendor/openplan3d, originating from OpenPlan3D, under the MIT license
      included in that folder (apps/plan-editor/vendor/openplan3d/LICENSE).

9. Termination

   If you breach this license, your rights under this license end automatically and immediately. The
   Licensor may reinstate them in writing. If it is your first breach and you stop it within 30 days after
   the Licensor notified you, your rights are reinstated.

10. No warranty and limited liability

   The Software is provided "as is", without any warranty, express or implied, including but not limited
   to warranties of merchantability, fitness for a particular purpose or non-infringement of third-party
   rights. The AREI findings in the Software are not an inspection and no guarantee that an installation
   complies with the regulations. To the extent permitted by law, the Licensor is not liable for any
   damage arising from the use of or the inability to use the Software. This limitation does not apply to
   wilful misconduct or fraud, or where the law prohibits a limitation.

11. Later versions

   The Licensor may distribute later versions of the Software under a different license or different
   terms. What you obtained under this license remains under this license for you, unless you accept the
   new terms.

12. Governing law and jurisdiction

   This license is governed by Belgian law. Disputes fall under the exclusive jurisdiction of the courts
   of the judicial district of the Licensor's domicile, without prejudice to mandatory rules that
   give jurisdiction to another court.

13. Contact

   Anyone who wants to use the Software in production, wants any other permission or a license, or has a
   question about this license, can contact the Licensor at steff@steffbeckers.com.
